[b]Cinematic Conversation Camera[/b]

Cut between the player and NPC during dialogue. Choose from 39 camera angles,
adjust each shot's field of view and movement, and set when the angle changes.

Choose Standard, Close or Room, or save your own presets. Keep Subject Visible
looks for a clear enabled shot and can switch to first person when the view is
blocked. Ignore Obstructions Mid-Shot holds the selected camera position.

Adjust letterbox bars, HUD visibility and dialogue fading. Inventory, barter
and other menus suspend the camera presentation until you close them.

[b]Player voice and expressions[/b]

DBVO 1, DBVO 2 and Dragonborn ReVoiced are detected automatically.
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/184221]Dragonborn ReVoiced[/url]
1.4.4 or newer is recommended for voice timing and player lip sync.
DBVO uses the optional Lip Sync Fallback. A voice mod is not required.

Responsive Expressions adds brow and squint movement while speaking and reactions
while listening. Eye & Cheek Detail needs a matching regional asset, supplied
separately. Voice tone and sarcasm are not analyzed.

[b]Requirements[/b]

Skyrim SE/AE, matching [url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE[/url] and
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library[/url].
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/120352]SKSE Menu Framework[/url]
is optional for the settings panel.

[b]Install[/b]

Close Skyrim and replace the old version through MO2 or Vortex.
Keep SD_user.ini to retain menu settings. No ESP or Papyrus scripts.
Nothing is written to your save.

[b]Settings[/b]

Open Cinematic Conversation Camera in SKSE Menu Framework, or edit
Data/SKSE/Plugins/SD.ini. Menu changes save to SD_user.ini.
Settings marked (restart) need a game restart.

The default is Close, with a new angle every 3–6 eligible lines, 12% letterbox
bars, dialogue fading, responsive expressions and DBVO lip-sync fallback.

[b]Compatibility[/b]

Keep SmoothCam enabled. The camera returns to it after dialogue.

For Improved Camera in first person, set bScripted=0 under [EVENTS] in
SKSE/Plugins/ImprovedCameraSE/Profiles/Default.ini, or your active profile.
This affects its other scripted forced-third-person events too.
Third-person players do not need the change.

Disable Improved Alternate Conversation Camera, Alternate Conversation Camera,
Switch Camera During Dialogue, and Camera Noise or other camera-shake mods.

[b]Version 1.5.0[/b]

Film other people's conversations: press Film Their Conversation, or turn on
Film When You Stand Still, and two NPCs talking are filmed like your own
conversation. Game scenes are filmed as a whole, and the camera lets go when
the scene hands you your turn.
Subtitles In The Black Bar: the spoken line sits inside the bottom bar (off by
default).
Hold On Their Answer: persuade, intimidate or bribe, and their answer gets a
close-up with a slow push in.
Preset files: export your settings from the Presets page and share them as a
mod; installed presets show up in the same list.
Close-ups follow the face, NPCs at workbenches stop working to talk, and the
extreme close-ups now crop below the chin. NPCs no longer snap into place when
the camera cuts to them.
The Release build and 24 tests pass.

Settings and compatibility details are in USAGE.md in the download.
Logs are in Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/SceneDirector.log.

[b]Source and license[/b]

GPL-3.0-or-later with the included exceptions. Dependency licenses and credits
are in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and licenses/.
Download the matching complete Source.zip from the same release.

